  "notes": "Used for authoritative leadership of organized groups. The two main domains are organizational/military command and musical conducting.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {部隊|ぶたい}を{指揮|しき}する: to command troops\n- オーケストラを{指揮|しき}する: to conduct an orchestra\n- {作戦|さくせん}を{指揮|しき}する: to direct an operation\n- {指揮|しき}{者|しゃ}: conductor; commander\n- {指揮|しき}{官|かん}: commanding officer\n- {指揮|しき}{系統|けいとう}: chain of command\n- {指揮|しき}{棒|ぼう}: baton (conductor's)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {統率|とうそつ}する: to lead, command — emphasizes bringing a group together\n- {監督|かんとく}する: to supervise, direct — emphasizes overseeing\n- {率|ひき}いる: to lead — literary, used for leading groups of people",
